  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe commercial driver attends after a long shift with a folder containing a current signed letter, older screening paperwork and a handwritten personal account, and the nurse reconstructs the chronology before recording the present findings; differences between the records are described explicitly rather than resolved by treating the newest-looking photocopy as automatically authoritative.\n\nThe specialist's completed investigation found no diagnosable cause for a single confirmed blackout, and the signed chronology documents one event with no further events over 4.9 years; the nurse records that this is a blackout of undetermined nature after investigation, rather than an investigation still pending, while an earlier faint in the driver's father is kept separate from the patient's event count and cannot create a recurrent patient history.\n\nThe employer's copied form relates to an earlier period of work and contains a broad satisfactory box without the measurements underlying it, whereas the current nurse entry identifies the source of each specific finding; the driver's wish to continue scheduled duties is recorded as a preference, not as proof that the present assessment has resolved the documented concern.\n\nBefore closing the interview, the nurse checks that the driver's recollection and the supplied clinical document have not been merged into a single undated finding, and records the outstanding documents separately; the completed entries remain current findings, while any missing qualification, conflicting detail or unperformed examination stays available for review rather than being silently treated as normal.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
